draftRequest.text:
Implement these Draft Cards in {where}, matching each one's description, content, provisional ports and the existing connections, and keeping the Card ids and wiring. Use a built-in Card where it is enough (data already in the project is handed on by an input Card with a File output; see the rules), otherwise a code Card (language, default.nix, sources and _outputs.fbs). Look at the bundled demos with reference_read when unsure how to write something, and check planned changes with project_validate {"changes": [...]} instead of saving trials.
Work one Card at a time, upstream first: check it with project_validate, save it, run the workflow from its trigger Card, and confirm the Card's result with run_record before going on to the next. At the end, report what each Card does and what the run produced.
{list}
